00:05:37,894 --> 00:05:43,894
He's got a lot on his mind.

2
00:11:15,789 --> 00:11:21,789
Greenberg is a comedy, drama, romance film directed by Noah Baumbach.

3
00:16:53,684 --> 00:16:59,684
Roger Greenberg, a failed musician now making a living as a carpenter in New
York, returns to Los Angeles to house-sit for his brother.

4
00:22:31,578 --> 00:22:37,578
He's stranded there—since he doesn't drive—until his
brother's assistant, Florence, comes to his rescue.

5
00:28:09,473 --> 00:28:15,473
She's as much a lost soul as he is, and the pair form a significant
connection—giving Roger a much-needed reason to be happy.

6
00:33:47,368 --> 00:33:53,368
Roger Greenberg, played by Ben Stiller.

7
00:39:25,263 --> 00:39:31,263
Florence Marr, played by Greta Gerwig.

8
00:45:03,157 --> 00:45:09,157
Ivan Schrank, played by Rhys Ifans.

9
00:50:41,052 --> 00:50:47,052
Beth (Beller's Party), played by Jennifer Jason Leigh.

10
00:56:18,947 --> 00:56:24,947
Eric Beller (Beller's Party), played by Mark Duplass.

11
01:01:56,842 --> 01:02:02,842
Gina, played by Merritt Wever.

12
01:07:34,736 --> 01:07:40,736
Greenberg is a 2010 American romantic comedy-drama film directed by Noah Baumbach, who wrote
the screenplay and co-wrote the story with his then-wife Jennifer Jason Leigh.

13
01:13:12,631 --> 01:13:18,631
The film stars Ben Stiller, Greta Gerwig, Rhys Ifans, and Leigh, with Mark Duplass, Merritt Wever, Chris
Messina, Brie Larson, Juno Temple, Jake Paltrow, and Dave Franco in supporting roles.

14
01:18:50,526 --> 01:18:56,526
The film's soundtrack features the first film score by James Murphy.

15
01:24:28,421 --> 01:24:34,421
The film had its world premiere at the 60th Berlin
International Film Festival on February 14, 2010.

16
01:30:06,315 --> 01:30:12,315
Distributed by Focus Features, Greenberg began a limited theatrical release in New York City and Los
Angeles on March 19, 2010, followed by a wide release in the United States on March 26.

17
01:35:44,210 --> 01:35:50,210
It received positive reviews from critics and grossed $7
million worldwide against a budget of $25 million.

18
01:41:22,105 --> 01:41:28,105
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
